            <ArticleTitle>[The chronobiological aspects of drug resistance to antianginal therapy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two groups of ischemic heart disease patients with different responses to antianginal therapy (propranolol, nifedipine) were studied. Mathematical analysis of heart rate variabilities showed that tolerant patients had a low index of centralization, lack of its circadian rhythm and a low correlation between several cardiointervalographic parameters. Bearing in mind these shifts makes it possible to predict the therapeutical efficiency of the antianginal drugs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
